{"reference":"Proverbs 29","book":"Proverbs","chapter":29,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Justice and Material Outcomes","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Proverbs does not treat material outcomes as the result of diligence and personal choice alone. It also condemns bribery and rulers who deny justice. Proverbs 29:4 sets a king's justice against one who exacts gifts, presenting public stability as bound up with just rule.","verse_refs":["Proverbs 29:4"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_proverbs_029_e6929c840c9a2e99e8a747a5"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}